{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>As much as the tread of a foot.</b> Even the tread of the sole of a foot — that is, even the trampling of a foot I do not permit you to pass through their land without permission. And its midrash aggadah: until there comes the day of the tread of the sole of a foot on the Mount of Olives, as it says (Zechariah 14): ״וְעָמְדוּ רַגְלָיו״ and so forth." "<b>As a possession to Esau.</b> From Abraham — ten nations I gave him: seven to you, and Keni and Kenizi and Kadmoni, who are Ammon and Moab and Seir; one of them to Esau and two to the sons of Lot, as reward that he went with him to Egypt and kept silent about what he was saying about his wife, ״she is my sister״ — he treated him as his son (Bereshit Rabbah 51)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:41.208461483Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}